# AAL v1.3 Agent Directive

When editing a file with AAL domain annotations (`# @!code-review`, `# @!testing`, etc.):

1. Respect the **effective annotation** at the edit line (file-level or function-level override).
2. Domain skills live under `.cursor/skills/<domain>/SKILL.md` — hooks inject them automatically on Write/Edit.
3. Do not remove or relocate `# @!domain` lines unless explicitly migrating annotations.
4. After changing domains or skills, run `axiompy-skills verify-domains --strict`.
5. New files: use `axiompy-skills annotate FILE --domain NAME` or add `# @!domain` at file top.

**Domains** map to bundled AxiomPy skills: `code-review`, `code-style`, `design-patterns`, `documentation`, `ship-it`, `testing`.

If inject fails (unknown domain, missing skill), fix the registry with `axiompy-skills install --project --hooks` or `axiompy-skills doctor --strict`.
